  "notes": "GAAP (modified accrual) per the combined Statement of Governmental Fund Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances and Statement of Activities (p2, original report p7, gained in the v7 re-trim). Receipts/disbursements and fund balances (1,055,004 / 859,435) from its Total governmental funds column (General + Construction); the reconciling-items and Statement of Activities columns are not used (net position 536,699 beginning / 3,540,504 ending; depreciation 547,615 and bond interest 39,096 appear only there; the Total column prints '---' for bond interest). Warrants issued 1,108,322 + bond issuance 3,325,000 = debt_proceeds 4,433,322 (computed). Roll-forward: 1,055,004+1,208,967-5,837,858+4,433,322=859,435. Collection fees and the delinquent tax allowance are printed as negative revenue lines and kept so (property tax, review). Placement fees and bond issue costs as debt service fees. Previously (old trim had only Schedule 1) receipts/disbursements came from Schedule 1 and its budgetary fund balances 1,042,807 / 879,213 were used as beginning/ending cash; those Schedule 1 lines now sit in detail (budgetary basis, Actual and budget columns, p3; Schedule 1 shows bond proceeds 3,192,000 vs 3,325,000 bond issuance on the GAAP statement), and beginning cash is null (no prior-year balance sheet). Read pages 1-3 of 3. Balance sheet from the combined Balance Sheet - Governmental Funds and Statement of Net Position (p1, original report p6, gained in the v8 re-trim), Statement of Net Position column (warrants and bonds split by the printed due dates; accrued interest as accrued liabilities; fund-column deferred revenue and fund balances reconcile to '---' there). ending_cash = Cash on deposit with County Treasurer 241,012 and ending_investments = Investments 643,681 (Total governmental funds column, same as the Statement of Net Position column)."
